# Defect 072's crossed program, which is what the narrowing makes REFUSABLE.
#
# Before panel 170 narrowed `one_tag_one_type` at `tag void`, the two families
# below had no tag to differ by, so the rule collapsed them onto ONE Heroes type
# and these two lines were an ordinary call: `check` 0, `build` 0, `run` 0, the
# arena destroyed, the heap block leaked, and the handle live set silent because
# the count balanced.
#
# The sibling case in `tests/golden/run/` is the MATCHED program — the one the
# author meant and could not write — and `ffi-handle-refusals.hero` beside this
# file still asserts that two handles over a REAL tag are `duplicate_tag`. The
# rule is intact everywhere it has a tag to work with; it is stood down on the
# one tag where no author can spell the difference.
#
# No header is needed: the refusal is a Heroes type error and never reaches
# clang, which is the whole point — `void *` and `void *` are one C type, so
# clang could not have caught either line.

extern "two-void-families.h"
    record Arena tag void
    record Heap tag void
    function arena_new() -> Arena acquires arena_free
    function arena_free(b: Arena consumes)
    function heap_new() -> Heap acquires heap_free
    function heap_free(b: Heap consumes)

function main()
    a = arena_new()
    h = heap_new()

    #~v type_mismatch
    heap_free(b: a)

    #~v type_mismatch
    arena_free(b: h)
